  "generated_text": "First, use the distributive property to expand the product:\n\n\\[\n(x^2-2x+2)(x^2+2x+2)\n\\]\n\nDistribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial:\n\n\\[\nx^2(x^2 + 2x + 2) - 2x(x^2 + 2x + 2) + 2(x^2 + 2x + 2)\n\\]\n\nNow, distribute each term:\n\n\\[\nx^4 + 2x^3 + 2x^2 - 2x^3 - 4x^2 - 4x + 2x^2 + 4x + 4\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\nx^4 + (2x^3 - 2x^3) + (2x^2 - 4x^2 + 2x^2) + (-4x + 4x) + 4\n\\]\n\nSo, the expanded form of the given product is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{x^4 - 2x^2 + 4}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[x**4 - 1*2*x**2 + 4, 'x^4 - 2x^2 + 4']",
    "gold_answer": "By the distributive property, this is equivalent to: $$x^2(x^2+2x+2)-2x(x^2+2x+2)+2(x^2+2x+2)$$Now, we can distribute in each of the above, and group like terms: $$x^4+2x^3+2x^2-2x^3-4x^2-4x+2x^2+4x+4$$$$\\boxed{x^4+4}$$",
    "is_correct": false
  },
